 is clearly  demonstrated in the trailer when we see  Celia opening up an iron door to release  the blue-haired God many descendants  fans believe Hades to be mouths father  after all she did refer to a blue orb as  dad in under the sea a descendent story  and since Hades is one of the newest  additions to the descendants franchise  fans are convinced that there's more to  his story than meets the eye  oddly enough Hades did have a daughter  named Macario and while we believe her  mother to be Persephone some sources  state that no one knows who her mother  truly is she's described as having black  hair and violet eyes and she's often  pictured wearing dark purples and greens  we don't know about you but this sounds  like a lot like mal to us still there's  a reason why Maleficent doesn't want her  daughter knowing who her father is  because well if a tease truly is her dad  this would make mal a demigod and since  Maleficent didn't want her daughter  knowing she was stronger than her this  may be why she chose to leave her in the  dark Disney's Hercules portrays Hades as  a gray skinned villain who has yellow  eyes a long face and flaming blue hair  he's short-tempered witty and bitter but  he's an honest God who always holds up  his end of the bargain he's often seen  wearing black robes that are tied  together with a silver skull pin going  from a cartoon to a real-life human can  be quite the jump which is why it's only  normal that actor Cheyenne Jackson looks  nothing like Disney's first adaptation  of the villain the Disney Channel has  managed to stay true to Hades essence  choosing to stick with the blue hair  wicked smile and black clothing still  ladies looks a lot more fashionable than  ever before do you think Hades will  prove himself useful and help the v-j  save auradon or is Hades truly as rotten  as they say he is the villain might  actually prove himself to be genuine and  kind however if they choose to base  Hades off of his Disney movie  counter